entry.summary:
🔥 A Quick Introduction to Routes in Laravel + Free Practical Project
In Laravel, Routes help us define how our application should respond when a user calls a URL through a browser.
Simple example:
Route::get('/about', function () {
    return 'This is About Page';
});

Route::get() : To receive data
Route::post() : To send data (forms)
Route::put() : To edit data
Route::delete() : To delete data
Laravel allows you to group routes:
Route::prefix('admin')->group(function () {
    Route::get('/dashboard', [DashboardController::class, 'index']);
});

I created a complete project using Laravel API Routes and JWT authentication that you can use for free and learn how to:
Create API Routes,
Implement authentication and protection of Routes,
and develop a real RESTful API.
